        "The Rise of Online Research and Its Benefits",
        "You are a methods instructor preparing a lesson on why psychological researchers moved their studies online. Trace the growth of internet research from the mid-1990s through the 2015 estimate that only 43 percent of samples were college students, and describe the benefits of online research: accessibility, efficient collection of large samples, greater sample diversity, remote participation, and easier sharing of study materials. Then argue how these advantages support replicability and generalizability while acknowledging the push for preregistration to reduce researcher flexibility.",
