            "Server-side programming (e.g., PHP, NodeJS, Django) more directly connects the web browser to the server and is used to store and send information back to users, whereas client-side programming (e.g., JavaScript) is code that is downloaded and run on a participant's computer.",
            "Existing tools that use JavaScript, such as jsPsych and PsychoJS, can be used to program experimental features such as random assignment.",
